WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.900
A note on the fridge door:

2
00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:04.510
«Il faut que tu viennes.»
You have to come.

3
00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:09.670
«viennes»? That isn't the «tu»
form of «venir» you learnt.

4
00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:11.780
So where did it come from?

5
00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:15.910
It gets stranger: «Il faut que
la société fasse plus.» «fasse»?

6
00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:19.950
From «faire»? It doesn't
look like any form you know.

7
00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:23.760
So why does French change
the verb after «il faut que»,

8
00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.100
and how do you build the new form?

9
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:29.370
In this mission, you'll watch
Mission D2's machine cut

10
00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:31.240
a verb and rebuild it.

11
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:35.360
Then you'll snap stems and
endings together in Mission I1.

12
00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:40.030
Your mission: explain why the
verb changes after «il faut que»,

13
00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:41.640
and build the new forms.
